# Merge gate (tvscreener-rs) - gRoussac Approve

tvscreener-rs is **not** agent-auto-merge. Same habit as **itcy-publications** BAT: Greg Approves, then merge.

## GitHub enforcement (locked)

Org branch protection on **`dev`** (Interchouette-ITC):

| Setting | Value |
| --- | --- |
| Required approving reviews | **1** |
| Require code owner review | **yes** (`CODEOWNERS` → `@gRoussac`) |
| Dismiss stale reviews | **yes** |
| Enforce for admins | **yes** |
| Allow force pushes | **no** |

Chat phrases like “merge whatever” / “just merge” do **not** override this. If `gh pr merge` succeeds with zero Approves, protection is broken: **stop and fix protection**, do not celebrate.

## Merge

| Repo | Agent duty |
| --- | --- |
| **tvscreener-rs** | Open/update PRs green + up to date; always `--reviewer gRoussac`. **Do not merge** until `reviews` show **APPROVED** from **gRoussac**. Then `gh pr merge --squash`. |

- Comments / review threads = babysit (fix, rework, Q&A). **Not** the merge gate.
- Do **not** ask "OK to merge?" in chat as a substitute for GitHub Approve.
- Do **not** `gh pr merge --rebase` onto org (strips Verified). Rebase on the **fork** first; then squash-merge after Approve.
- After merge: sync fork `dev` from `upstream/dev` as usual.
- Full checklist: `github-public-quality.mdc` + `github-fork-pr.mdc`.

## Pre-merge check (required)

Before every `gh pr merge`:

```bash
gh pr view <n> --repo Interchouette-ITC/tvscreener-rs --json reviews,reviewRequests,state
# Must see: reviews[].state == APPROVED AND reviews[].author.login == gRoussac
```

If no `APPROVED` from **gRoussac**: **do not merge**. Leave the PR open.

## Seeing approvals

```bash
gh pr view <n> --repo Interchouette-ITC/tvscreener-rs --json reviews,reviewRequests,state
# reviews[].state == APPROVED, reviews[].author.login == gRoussac
```

## Still ask Greg when

- Secrets, logins, installs needing approval.
- Explicit hold he set in chat or on the PR (beyond the standing Approve gate).
- Changing org branch protection settings.
